You are given a differential game logic (dGL) loop and a desired postcondition that Angel (the controller) aims to maintain.
An inductive invariant has already been established, but we want to expand it to cover a larger set of conditions where Angel can maintain controllability.

You have a plan describing the Angel's control strategy to remain safe under broadened initial conditions by expanding the loop invariant, as well as some intermediate conditions that characterize these broadened initial conditions.
Finally, you also have bounds on various variables that you can plug into the intermediate conditions.
Your task is to put the pieces together and output a single strengthened loop invariant formula based on the provided information.

